  "heat": 3,
  "text": "She gave him milk, tucked him in, then finished the war… … Sisera has been crushing Israel for twenty years with 900 iron chariots. His army finally collapses and he’s running for his life on foot. He ducks into the nearest tent. A woman named Jael comes out all soft: “Turn in, my lord. Fear not.” He asks for water. She gives him milk. Covers him up. He falls asleep. Then she takes a tent peg and a hammer… and goes softly. Walks out, finds the commander hunting him, and says “Come, I’ll show you the man you’re looking for.” The victory song calls her blessed above women. And it ends with Sisera’s mother waiting at the window wondering why his chariot is taking so long while her friends reassure her he’s just dividing the girls. She served milk and a murder. I’m scared of her and I love her. ---",
